  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14158570/assets/f6f2ce8adb8c1b35c2fd4928805f486920228b913c3a7fc18ddc60b26a8e8fcd.png)\n\nLet $X$ be a random variable with the probability density function shown above. What are the modes of $X?$",
  "worked_solution": "The modes of a random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ are the values of $x$ at the global maxima of $f(x).$\n\nFrom the graph, we can tell that the global maxima of $f(x)$ are at $x=5,7.$\n\nTherefore, the modes of $X$ are $5$ and $7.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14158570/assets/59b72efa72dd48bc2fb74fed5f795341f59af377af0756965abab9d23390d468.png)",
